            <ArticleTitle>Eruptive milia during isotretinoin therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>728-729</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/pde.13270</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Isotretinoin (13-cis-retinoic acid) is a synthetic vitamin A derivative that is effective in the treatment of recalcitrant, nodulocystic acne. To our knowledge, there are no reports in the medical literature of milia as a side effect of isotretinoin. We report a case of eruptive facial milia in the setting of isotretinoin treatment for acne.</AbstractText>
